# Internal planning material: session plans and design notes. They are working notes, not
# documentation, and describe the module as it was mid-development rather than as it ships. They
# stay on the maintainer's disk, ignored. Add an explicit negation below for a file genuinely meant
# to be tracked.
docs/superpowers/

# docs/live-verification/ is where live tenant console output is pasted in on purpose. It holds
# the placeholder register today; the checklists arrive with the first live-verified change. No
# rule above reaches it. Redaction is done on the way INTO a checklist there, gated by
# tests/QA/dochygiene.tests.ps1. These two rules cover the raw material that redaction is done
# FROM, so an unredacted transcript cannot be staged by a stray `git add docs/`.
docs/live-verification/raw/
docs/live-verification/*.log

# Claude Code's per-clone session state -- machine-local session ids and absolute temp paths, of no
# value to anyone else and stale the moment it is shared.
.claude/

# Neither block untracks anything: .gitignore never does. The checklists that will live under
# docs/live-verification/ stay tracked deliberately -- they are the verification record, and only
# the raw material beside them is ignored.
